  "testDataReadinessSummary": {"executable": 12, "externalFixtureRequired": 0, "reviewRequired": 0, "note": "All Appendix O rules validate format/structure/algorithm only; none require a live token vault, real tokenization service, or cryptographic verification to be meaningfully tested."},
  "testDataStatus": "AppendixOPaymentTokenTerminologyValidator independently implements and tests all seven BRs (13-19 digit token representation, LUHN check digit, token-vs-PAN inequality, token expiration YYMM format, 28/56-byte base64 cryptogram length, Token Data Block A/B framing, and POS Entry Mode code recognition) with in-repo fixtures. No dedicated AI-generated tokenized artifact or token-BIN registry is available, so token-BIN-range designation, cryptographic cryptogram authenticity, and which specific POS Entry Mode codes represent token presentment remain explicitly out of scope rather than asserted. \"Payment Token Requestor\" and \"Payment Token Service Provider\" are pure glossary terms with no attached field format in the source and have no independently assertable check.",
  "remaining": ["Author specialized AI-generated tokenized artifacts (real token/cryptogram/entry-mode samples) to replace the in-repo synthetic fixtures before implementation certification.","Confirm the token BIN registry/designation rules, cryptographic cryptogram verification, and the exact POS Entry Mode code(s) that represent token presentment with the tokenization implementation.","Decide whether/how to wire AppendixOPaymentTokenTerminologyValidator into Segment100PayloadValidator if a modeled token/cryptogram field is ever added to the Segment 100 payload schema."]
